"Inside the Check-in Counter feels safe, like coming home, and smells of reeds on a lake."
"A break room off the hall holds a dead magical cooler and overgrown terrarium gardens."
"The break room's cupboards hold a large box of salt, which never spoils."
"The Library keeps roots and vegetables that are safe for a human to eat."
"Two short steps at the dark back of the hall lead up to a floor of more books and carved rails."
"Bookworms are grey worms a few inches long with rings of color at each end, and cute."
"Bookworms feed on magical residue, clean up book dust, and have affinities of their own."
"Bookworms are needed to make magical quills, and fertilise soil for magical herbs."
"Left untended for centuries, bookworms at the back of the hall have grown engorged and huge."
"The small engorged bookworms are the size of a small dog."
"An engorged bookworm at the back steps is six or seven feet long and waist high."
"The big engorged bookworm is bloated and matte grey, its colored mouth rings blotched."
"An engorged bookworm has no eyes, and a round mouth rimmed with rows of jagged teeth."
"An engorged bookworm rears up and roars a squelching challenge when it senses a Librarian."
"The Library shows the big bookworm as Engorged Bookworm, Status: Alert, Health: 100%."
"Engorged bookworms drain the Library's remaining energy as they devour its books."
"Salt dries a bookworm out and leaves it helpless, but the biggest are too big to pick up."
"Links hands a newcomer a broom as her first weapon against the bookworms."
"Links can rake a bookworm with his claws in lynx form, at a cost in power."
